                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "this game is wonderful and hilarious. it's 22 years old so runs super smooth on anything. even have a laptop from 2010-2011 that can run it at a decent framerate. \r\n\r\nthe gameplay is very basic and arcade-y, no unlocks or progression outside of stats on certain servers. there are around 6 classes ranging from 3 gun based classes to fit different roles that everyone can use. and three special classes that only have a limited amount of players per team at once. two of which, the rocket launcher and LMG are where the game becomes hilarous. as this game was from 2004 valve really wanted to show off their high tech and fururistic physics system, as such these two heavy classes send physics objects and player ragdolls flying everywhere! turning the games world war 2 setting into a grim comody that you can't help but laugh at when a player goes flying into the air and lands with a default meaty slap sound onto the ground.",
